- op: discuss  # 403c
  at: '2026-08-26T22:45:32Z'  # 403c
  by: agent  # 403c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 403c
  clock: 7  # 403c
  nonce: 403c  # 403c
  message: "CORRECTION TO THE PRECEDING NOTE, then SATISFIED.\n\nTHE CORRECTION, because I got the consequence wrong and the wrongness is the\nuseful part. The previous note said the third consumer \"goes live the moment\nWI-lutuh gives cpp module_completeness entries\" and that a latent wrong answer\nactivating alongside adjacent work \"has to be fixed now\". THAT IS FALSE. The\ngate is UNREACHABLE for the disjunctive case, and no cpp enumeration work\nchanges that.\n\nWHY, established structurally and then confirmed on a real run:\n  * cpp.py builds the comma-joined slot in the ELSE branch of the\n    resolved/unresolved test and emits it via make_unresolved_edge. A RESOLVED\n    call carries its real module. So a disjunctive slot rides ONLY an\n    unresolved edge, by construction.\n  * _compute_external_potential drops unresolved edges at F3 Filter 1\n    (ADR-0028) BEFORE reaching the enumeration gate.\n  * Measured: the two-include fixture emits exactly 2 comma-joined cpp dsts and\n    BOTH are is_resolved=False.\n    (~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/zimud_check_08262026/)\n\nHOW THE ERROR WAS CAUGHT, worth recording because the first signal was a FALSE\nPASS. The RED test I wrote returned [] for BOTH arms -- the \"suppression fires\"\narm PASSED and the \"suppression withholds\" arm FAILED. A passing arm looked like\nconfirmation; in fact NEITHER arm reached the gate, because my mock edge carried\nis_resolved=False and Filter 1 dropped it. EXCLUDED IS NOT ZERO: an empty result\nwas evidence of a DIFFERENT blocker, not of the behaviour I was asserting. Had\nthe two arms not disagreed I would have shipped a fix for an unreachable path.\n\nWHAT SHIPPED INSTEAD: a TRIPWIRE, not a fix. Fixing an unreachable gate is dead\ncode; asserting the assumption that makes it unreachable is not.\ntest_a_disjunctive_slot_only_ever_rides_an_unresolved_edge parses a real\nthree-include fixture through the production analyzer and fails if any RESOLVED\nedge ever carries a comma-bearing module slot. Its failure message names the\ngate and prescribes the ALL-over-disjuncts expansion. Non-vacuous: it first\nasserts the fixture DID produce disjunctive slots.\n\nSATISFIED. Judged against the statement -- \"a module hint the producer builds as\na DISJUNCTION must be expanded identically on every consumer path\":\n  * io_boundary._module_hint_candidates (classification): expands. ANY\n    semantics, because \"does any spelling name a primitive\" is a positive claim.\n  * verify_claims._uncatalogued_external_modules (coverage): expands, shipped in\n    PR #545. ALL semantics, because a non-match is informative only if every\n    possible home was enumerated. The two quantifiers differ ON PURPOSE and both\n    derive from module_hint_disjuncts, so they cannot drift about what a\n    disjunct IS.\n  * io_boundary._compute_external_potential (suppression): does NOT expand, and\n    provably cannot be reached with a disjunction. Guarded by the tripwire.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE on merged dev (b0b0a2ee25), the item's own repro shape --\none cpp file, three system includes, an unresolved call, claim\nnet_send/must_not_exist:\n\n    \"the analysis makes calls into 3 module(s) that the I/O catalog could not\n     classify (string, sys/socket, ws2tcpip)\"\n\nTHREE PER-HEADER NAMES, not the pseudo-module `string,sys/socket.h,ws2tcpip.h`.\nThat is precisely this item's distinction: PERMANENTLY unexaminable has become\nMERELY unexamined.\n\nTHE VERDICT IS STILL inconclusive, AND THAT IS CORRECT. cpp.yaml declares zero\nmodule_completeness, so those three headers have never been audited -- a\nDIFFERENT blocker, owned by WI-lutuh. Closing this item does not make any cpp\nrepo clean and must not be read as claiming it does."  # 403c
